<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's money supply up to $21.5 bln in April.</title>
<headline>Morocco's money supply up to $21.5 bln in April.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) released on Tuesday its latest statistics showing that money supply rose to 202.7 billion dirhams ($21.5 billion) in April against 186.5 billion dirhams in April 1996.</p>
<p>These are figures of Morocco's money supply in billions of dirhams at end period:</p>
<p>    1997	     M1	   M2	    M3</p>
<p>    April	  47.733     98.452	56.560</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    April	  44.133     92.284	50.144</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>    March	  46.180     99.072	56.554</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    March	  43.167     92.294	50.542</p>
<p>The bank defined the agregates as follows:</p>
<p>M1 -- Currency in circulation + Banks cash holdings.</p>
<p>M2 -- M1 + Money + Deposit accounts.</p>
<p>M3 -- M2 + Quasi-money.</p>
<p>($1= 9.4 dirhams)</p>
</text>
